1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,571
This guy told people a five hundred dollar loan would cost them six fifty. Then he took nineteen twenty-five.

2
00:00:06,521 --> 00:00:09,184
His name's Scott Tucker. Payday loans, online.

3
00:00:09,434 --> 00:00:13,142
The paperwork said: borrow five hundred, pay back six hundred fifty total.

4
00:00:13,442 --> 00:00:19,676
Every payday, the loan renewed by default. He'd pull out a hundred fifty in fees, and the five hundred you owed? Never moved.

5
00:00:19,976 --> 00:00:25,947
The Justice Department described one borrower who paid fourteen twenty-five in fees. On a five hundred dollar loan.

6
00:00:26,247 --> 00:00:28,319
That's about seven hundred percent a year.

7
00:00:29,219 --> 00:00:33,086
At least four and a half million borrowers. Over three and a half billion dollars.

8
00:00:33,986 --> 00:00:36,524
So where'd the money go? A pro racing team. His own.

9
00:00:36,824 --> 00:00:40,791
October twenty seventeen, a jury convicted him on all fourteen counts.

10
00:00:41,691 --> 00:00:46,599
The sentence? Two hundred months. That's sixteen— sixteen years and eight months.

11
00:00:46,949 --> 00:00:51,563
So if a small fee never makes the balance go down, what are you actually paying for? Comment.

12
00:00:52,127 --> 00:00:53,599
Follow for the next one.
